# Shipped Bash hooks/scripts MUST stay LF: under core.autocrlf these get CRLF on checkout, and a
# CRLF `\r` in a shebang/command breaks the hook on Linux/macOS (and Git-Bash). Force LF regardless.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Golden wire-capture oracles must never be line-ending normalized (they contain raw protobuf
# bytes, incl. 0x0a). Without this, autocrlf would corrupt them on checkout.
*.bin binary
tests/Clavity.Ls.Tests/TestData/** binary

# Shell scripts (e.g. shipped plugin hooks) must stay LF on every platform — a CRLF *.sh
# fails on Linux/macOS with "bad interpreter". Keeps the portable hooks runnable cross-OS.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Byte-determinism for the hash-pinned registrar: identical EOL in every checkout so the build-time SHA-256
# pin (register-plugin-hash.iss) matches the packed bytes the uninstaller verifies (GetSHA256OfFile). See
# docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-19-installer-registration-convergence.md Task 5.
installer/_shared/register-plugin.ps1 text eol=crlf
